L4  reading: the dipole's vertical component has the published sign (northern stars receding) at every
    mass, but the model's apex lies about 100 degrees from the published apex and the amplitude grows far
    more slowly than the mass. The rigid model is therefore NOT validated against the measured reflex.

L5  model-free ceiling: a pure dipole of amplitude A adds A^2 / 3 to a bin's variance. Removing a dipole of
    the full published reflex amplitude (PROVISIONAL, measured beyond 40 kpc) from each bin:
    A = 32 km/s: dispersions 95.47, 105.13, 90.76 (changes -1.77, -1.61, -1.86); excess 12.01 against 11.81
    A = 36 km/s: dispersions 95.00, 104.70, 90.25 (changes -2.25, -2.04, -2.36); excess 12.07 against 11.81
    a dipole in the 30-40 bin alone would need A = 85 km/s to carry the whole excess.
kappa = 1/2 FITTED; not theory closed. Adopts nothing.
